Short:        AGA graphics extension for AMOS Pro
Author:       HWARF (Jerome)
Uploader:     amethist rumor786 passinbox com (Jerome)
Type:         dev/amos
Version:      0.13.2 (R57, 12 Nov 2026)
Requires:     AMOS Professional and an AGA Amiga (or AGA-enabled WinUAE)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet

Description:
  AMOSPro AGA Extension is an unofficial extension for AMOS
  Professional on AGA-equipped Commodore Amiga computers, such
  as the A1200 and A4000, and on suitably configured WinUAE.

  It adds 53 native AMOS commands and functions for AGA graphics,
  without requiring a replacement for the original AMOS editor.

  Main features:
    - AGA indexed screens with 2 to 256 colours
    - IFF/ILBM picture loading and palette management
    - Double buffering and back-buffer drawing
    - Safe Blitter copy, fill and clear operations
      (R57 revised graphics.library fill/clear implementation)
    - Copper raster effects
    - 2D drawing: Plot, Draw, Box and Circle
    - Text rendering and AMOS font-bank selection
    - Keyboard and mouse input, including cursor visibility
      limited to the extension's own AGA window
    - AGAPAL palette banks, fades and palette cycling
    - AGAPIC compressed images in AMOS DATA banks, with CPU
      decoding, opaque/masked drawing and image capture
    - Bank-number convenience commands for images and fonts

  The cursor visibility command does not disable the Workbench
  pointer or mouse input in other windows.

  The R57 / v0.13.2 library has passed automated CPU/CI tests
  and WinUAE tests in both interpreted AMOS and newly compiled
  programs for the documented R57 scenarios.

  R57 improves back-buffer Fill and Clear performance. In one
  compiled WinUAE benchmark, median Fill time decreased from
  54 to 41 ticks and Clear from 115 to 58 ticks versus R55.
  These are emulator benchmark results, not measurements on
  physical Amiga hardware.

  Tests on a physical AGA Amiga have NOT yet been performed,
  and not every command combination has been exhaustively tested.

  Installation:
    1. Back up your existing AMOS configuration and libraries.
    2. Copy AMOSPro_AGA.Lib into your AMOS APSystem directory.
    3. In AMOS Professional, open Config / Set Interpreter /
       Set Loaded Extensions and register the library in a free
       extension slot (historically slot 14 in the project).
    4. Save the interpreter configuration and restart AMOS.
    5. Import .asc example files with Project / Merge ASCII.
       These files are plain text, not native tokenized .AMOS files.

  Some demos need the included IFF picture or font banks. See
  INSTALL.md and the examples documentation for details.

  Requirements:
    - AMOS Professional already installed
    - AGA chipset or AGA-enabled WinUAE configuration
    - An unused AMOS extension slot

  The code, native library, example source and technical
  documentation are released under the MIT License. Graphics,
  logos, IFF images and fonts have separate licensing terms;
  consult ASSETS_LICENSE.md and the relevant attribution files.

  Source, updates and documentation:
    https://github.com/anthea176/AMOSPro-AGA-Extension

  Developed by HWARF with assistance from ChatGPT (OpenAI) for
  programming, testing and documentation.
